 comparisons.</p><ul><li>Arbitrary real inner-product E, with no finite-dimension or measurability premise. Kappa&gt;=1 for the comparisons; the total definition accepts every real kappa.</li></ul><h3>Exact source metric/actual contraction</h3><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[Q_\kappa(x,p)=\left(\frac1{2\kappa}+\frac12\right)\|x\|^2+\langle x,p\rangle+\|p\|^2.\]</div><h2>Read the formalized proofs</h2><p>Each statement and proof below has its own closed Lean disclosure. Samplinglib parents, Mathlib calls and external mathematical sources are distinguished in each proof.</p><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.phaseQuadraticForm"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h2>For every real kappa and phase point, define the exact source block-matrix quadratic form Q_kappa</h2><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.phaseQuadraticForm</code> · def · <a href="../../../lessons/index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every real kappa and phase point, define the exact source block-matrix quadratic form Q_kappa. Valid norm use is restricted to kappa&gt;=1 by the compiled comparisons.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[Q_\kappa(x,p)=\left(\frac1{2\kappa}+\frac12\right)\|x\|^2+\langle x,p\rangle+\|p\|^2.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Evaluate the source block matrix</strong><p>Both off-diagonal entries are1/2, so their sum is the cross inner product. This reuses the existing definition unchanged; public visibility enables the actual numerical contraction consumer.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Arbitrary real inner-product E, with no finite-dimension or measurability premise. Kappa&gt;=1 for the comparisons; the total definition accepts every real kappa.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Construction and meaning</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Evaluate the source block matrix</h4><p>Both off-diagonal entries are1/2, so their sum is the cross inner product. This reuses the existing definition unchanged; public visibility enables the actual numerical contraction consumer.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\tfrac12\langle x,p\rangle+\tfrac12\langle p,x\rangle=\langle x,p\rangle.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>phaseQuadraticForm</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.phaseQuadraticForm"><summary>Lean statement · phaseQuadraticForm</summary><p>For every real kappa and phase point, define the exact source block-matrix quadratic form Q_kappa. Valid norm use is restricted to kappa&gt;=1 by the compiled comparisons.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">def phaseQuadraticForm (kappa : ℝ) (z : E × E) : ℝ</code></pre><p><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-phasemetric.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="Aut