3>Exact source metric/actual contraction</h3><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\|x\|^2+\|p\|^2\le6Q_\kappa(x,p).\]</div><h2>Read the formalized proofs</h2><p>Each statement and proof below has its own closed Lean disclosure. Samplinglib parents, Mathlib calls and external mathematical sources are distinguished in each proof.</p><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h2>For every real inner-product E, kappa&gt;=1 and phase point z, the true coordinate energy is bounded by6 times the exact source Q</h2><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm</code> · theorem · <a href="../../../lessons/index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every real inner-product E, kappa&gt;=1 and phase point z, the true coordinate energy is bounded by6 times the exact source Q.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\|x\|^2+\|p\|^2\le6Q_\kappa(x,p).\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Use the lower cross-term Cauchy bound</strong><p>inner(x,p)&gt;=-||x||||p||. The coefficient1/(2kappa) is nonnegative; expand6Q-energy and use the square(2||x||-3||p||)². The unchanged existing proof gives the uniform constant6, including zero displacement and dimension.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Arbitrary real inner-product E, with no finite-dimension or measurability premise. Kappa&gt;=1 for the comparisons; the total definition accepts every real kappa.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Use the lower cross-term Cauchy bound</h4><p>inner(x,p)&gt;=-||x||||p||. The coefficient1/(2kappa) is nonnegative; expand6Q-energy and use the square(2||x||-3||p||)². The unchanged existing proof gives the uniform constant6, including zero displacement and dimension.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\langle x,p\rangle\ge-\|x\|\|p\|,\quad(2\|x\|-3\|p\|)^2\ge0.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>abs_real_inner_le_norm; sq_nonneg; nlinarith</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm"><summary>Lean statement · ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm</summary><p>For every real inner-product E, kappa&gt;=1 and phase point z, the true coordinate energy is bounded by6 times the exact source Q.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm {kappa : ℝ} (hkappa : 1 ≤ kappa)
    (z : E × E) :
    ‖z.1‖ ^ 2 + ‖z.2‖ ^ 2 ≤ 6 * phaseQuadraticForm kappa z</code></pre><p><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-phasemetric.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm"><summary>Lean proof · ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm</summary><p>Exact source form and compiled parent composition, with all source domains/constant absorption and zero cases explicit. Existing Q/comparison proofs unchanged.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm {kappa : ℝ} (hkappa : 1 ≤ kappa)
    (z : E × E) :
    ‖z.1‖ ^ 2 + ‖z.2‖ ^ 2 ≤ 6 * phaseQuadraticForm kappa z := by
  have hkappa0 : 0 &lt; kappa := lt_of_lt_of_le zero_lt_one hkappa
  have hinner : -(‖z.1‖ * ‖z.2‖) ≤ inner ℝ z.1 z.2 :=
    (abs_le.mp (abs_real_inner_le_norm z.1 z.2)).1
  have hcoef0 : 0 ≤ 1 / (2 * kappa) := by positivity
  rw [phaseQuadraticForm]
  nlinarith [mul_nonneg hcoef0 (sq_nonneg ‖z.1‖),
    sq_nonneg (2 * ‖z.1‖ - 3 * ‖z.2‖)]</code></pre><p><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-phasemetric.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><section data-source-comparison="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PhaseMetric.ordinary_energy_le_phaseQuadraticForm"><h3>Source assumptions versus formal assumptions</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Actual Lean</th><th>Difference kind</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Finite Euclidean source domain with the exact M_kappa block form.</td><td>Arbitrary real inner-product E, with no finite-dimension or measurability premise. Kappa&gt;=1 for the comparisons; the total definition accepts every real kappa.</td><td>generalization</td><td>Real inner-product presentation preserves the exact source form. Background comparisons need neither finite dimension nor measurable structure; nonlinear algorithm uses complete finite E and BorelSpace.</td></tr><tr><td>Universal c and C in the source Proposition4.7 step/contraction.</td><td>For every real inner-product E, kappa&gt;=1 and phase point z, the true coordinate energy is bounded by6 times the exact source Q.</td><td>source-implicit</td><td>Explicit conservative c=1/65536 is proved using the actual C8 algorithm remainder and source drift. Q/API definitions and comparison proofs are unchanged, with no extra completed-paper credit.</td></tr><tr><td>Actual V_eta from Lemma4.1.</td><td>Genuine global C2 f with explicit normalized curvature for the nonlinear consumer.</td><td>unresolved</td><td>The source smoothing/C2/curvature producer must be joined before claiming Proposition4.7 at V_eta or the full main result. Definitions and energy comparisons are already exact and independent of that producer.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Existing source Q/API promotion with unchanged proof, no separate mathematical progress credit. Actual