er-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For the actual normalized Gibbs law, its Gaussian smoothing and standard-Gaussian momentum, the q=2 squared M-kappa transport initialization cost is at most 5 kappa d, with the minimizer derived rather than assumed.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[W_{2,M_\kappa}^{2}(\delta_{x_{\rm ref}}\otimes\gamma,(\pi*\mathsf N(0,\eta I))\otimes\gamma)\le5\kappa d,\qquad\kappa=1/\alpha.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Convert Hessian curvature to strong convexity</strong><p>The genuine C2 Hessian lower bound implies whole-space strong convexity with the same alpha.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Construct the source minimizer</strong><p>Positive strong convexity and differentiability supply a global minimizer p with zero gradient; p is not added as a theorem hypothesis.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Apply the verified numerical transport chain</strong><p>The constructed critical point is fed to the already verified Gibbs moment, smoothing and identical-momentum coupling theorem.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>E is a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product Borel space.</li><li>U is C2 with alpha I &lt;= Hessian U &lt;= I and 0 &lt; alpha &lt;= 1.</li><li>The reference point has squared gradient norm at most alpha times dimension.</li><li>The smoothing variance eta lies in [0,1].</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Convert Hessian curvature to strong convexity</h4><p>The genuine C2 Hessian lower bound implies whole-space strong convexity with the same alpha.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[D^2U(x)\succeq\alpha I\Longrightarrow U\text{ is }\alpha\text{-strongly convex}.\]</div><details><summa