No supplied proximal point, law identity, normalizer, probability, curvature, gradient or moment certificate. Actual p, mu/R/r probability, normalized affine law, C2 curvature/mode and genuine position/Fisher L2 are internally produced. The numerical-prox eta&lt;=1/(2beta) cap is a separate computational contract.</td><td>generalization</td><td>Disclose finite Hilbert/Borel incl0 and measurable parameter-space extensions. Canonical affine identity is more general and does not assert probability; actual source consumer produces probability and moments.</td></tr><tr><td>Printed density proportionality and position IBP omit full normalization/regularity details.</td><td>Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0&lt;=Hessrho&lt;=etaI and I&lt;=HessQ&lt;=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr&lt;=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr&lt;=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.</td><td>source-implicit</td><td>Actual Haar Jacobian and constant cancellation are internally proved; exact noncompact IBP producer is reused. No normalizer/law/moment certificate is added.</td></tr><tr><td>First W2 comparison4.6, bias/MGF/fullLemma4.2, higher/Picard/Wp/warmness, main results and expected query costs.</td><td>Allpositive eta source3.2/4.4/4.5 plus true normalized affine posterior and lastTWO4.6 only. FIRSTW2 GaussianT2/LSI,bias4.2,centeredMGF4.3,fullLemma4.2,actual jointposterior Markov sampling/Picard/Wp/warmness/main/initialization/work/composition OPEN. Numericalprox cap eta&lt;=1/(2beta) is separate. TV never transfers unboundedcost.</td><td>unresolved</td><td>The last TWO squared comparisons alone do not establish W2 or full Lemma4.2. No numerical-prox cap, algorithm/work or TV-to-unbounded-cost transfer is claimed.</td></tr><tr><td>Section3.1 eta&gt;0 and Lemma4.2 have no upper eta bound; neighboring Lemma4.1 alone requires eta&lt;=1.</td><td>All eta(s)&gt;0, with no hsmall cap; every other sealed binder and output is unchanged.</td><td>same</td><td>The prior bounded analytic slice is preserved in immutable snapshots, but its cap is removed by a real internal allpositive measurable proximal producer. No producer estimate becomes a public premise.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Allpositive eta source3.2/4.4/4.5 plus true normalized affine posterior and lastTWO4.6 only. FIRSTW2 GaussianT2/LSI,bias4.2,centeredMGF4.3,fullLemma4.2,actual jointposterior Markov sampling/Picard/Wp/warmness/main/initialization/work/composition OPEN. Numericalprox cap eta&lt;=1/(2beta) is separate. TV never transfers unboundedcost.</p><p><strong>Encoder–denoiser:</strong> accepted · equivalent-after-elaboration</p><p>A generalization is not a source correction. Proposed missing conditions require separate independent repair review. No proposed repair silently changes the original theorem.</p></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Allpositive eta source3.2/4.4/4.5 plus true normalized affine posterior and lastTWO4.6 only. FIRSTW2 GaussianT2/LSI,bias4.2,centeredMGF4.3,fullLemma4.2,actual jointposterior Markov sampling/Picard/Wp/warmness/main/initialization/work/composition OPEN. Numericalprox cap eta&lt;=1/(2beta) is separate. TV never transfers unboundedcost.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-fullrangeproximalgaussianoracle.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-fullrangeproximalgauss-dbde54b019"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.FullRangeProximalGaussianOracle.full_range_proximal_gaussian_oracle</code></a></li><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-gibbspositionmoment.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-gibbspositionmoment-gi-b96deee0b7"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.GibbsPositionMoment.gibbs_position_moment</code></a></li><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-strongconvexgibbsintegrability.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-strongconvexgibbsintegrabili-51ed1587ae"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.StrongConvexGibbsIntegrability.integrable_exp_neg_of_strongConvexOn</code></a></li><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-hessianstrongconvexity.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-hessianstrongconvexity-stron-258a330876"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower</code></a></li><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-quadraticregularization.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-quadraticregularization-stro-17eea540ae"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic</code></a></li><li><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs.html#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs-map-affine-gibbs-afbd3acbfc"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>tilted_tilted</li><li>tilted_const</li><li>isProbabilityMeasure_tilted</li><li>HasFDerivAt.comp</li><li>HasFDerivAt.norm_sq</li><li>inner_gradient_left</li><li>integral_mono</li><li>integral_const_mul</li><li>memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8">SPHMC Ex8/p4.2/p4.3 and scoped4.6; affine prerequisite</a> — Allpositive eta source3.2/4.4/4.5 plus true normalized affine posterior and lastTWO4.6 only. FIRSTW2 GaussianT2/LSI,bias4.2,centeredMGF4.3,fullLemma4.2,actual jointposterior Markov sampling/Picard/Wp/warmness/main/initialization/work/composition OPEN. Numericalprox cap eta&lt;=1/(2beta) is separate. TV never transfers unboundedcost.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article><h3>Which proof obligations and prerequisites are covered?</h3><ul><li><span class="status status-orange">Formalized proof edge; source adapter/review separate</span> True standardized RGO and last TWO4.6 comparisons</li><li><span class="status status-red">TODO — not closed by these contributions</span> First W2 comparison, bias/MGF and full Lemma4.2 remaining</li><li><span class="status status-red">TODO — not closed by these contributions</span> Both main results and actual-input expected-query-cost composition remaining</li></ul></section><section id="sphmc-standardized-rgo-relative-entropy" data-publication-item="sphmc-standardized-rgo-relative-entropy"><h2>True standardized RGO unique proximal point and finite canonical entropy</h2><p>Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu, Matthew S. Zhang. Internally authored entropy/coherence background for the printed GaussianLSI/T2 invocation, not a separately printed theorem or full inequality.</p><p><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8">arXiv:2609.06906v1 with pinned Mathlib db584cd6 · S3.E2/S4.Ex3 actual proximal point; S4.Ex8 standardized posterior; S4.SS1.p4.2-p4.3/FIRST S4.E6 omitted canonical entropy domains.</a> · faithful paraphrase</p><h3>Complete source statement (Samplinglib restatement)</h3><p>Under unchanged normalized source curvature and C2 assumptions, produce the measurable uniquely stationary proximal point and the true affine standardized posterior; prove canonical KL finite, canonical llr L1 and only AE equality with the literal logdensity, actual residual L1 and both exact real entropy identities for every eta&gt;0.</p><ul><li>Complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, including dimension zero; canonical volume and covariance-I Gaussian.</li><li>Source kappa&gt;=1 and actual global C2 V with Hessian kappa^-1 I..I; positive eta. No supplied selector, probability, normalizer, integrability, entropy, LSI/T2 or final comparison certificate.</li><li>Authored measurable family S with measurable eta/y, every eta(s)&gt;0. Constant Unit specializes printed fixed parameters. Stationary uniqueness is an internally proved conclusion.</li></ul><h3>True standardized RGO unique proximal point and finite canonical entropy</h3><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[p_s+\eta_s\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\quad\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)&lt;\infty,\quad\log\frac{dr_s}{d\gamma}=\log q_s\quad r_s\text{-a.e.},\quad\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)=\int q_s\log q_s\,d\gamma=-\mathbb E_{r_s}\rho_s-\log Z_s.\]</div><h2>Read the formalized proofs</h2><p>Each statement and proof below has its own closed Lean disclosure. Samplinglib parents, Mathlib calls and external mathematical sources are distinguished in each proof.</p><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h2>True standardized RGO unique proximal point and finite canonical entropy</h2><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy</code> · theorem · <a href="../../../lessons/index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">Under unchanged normalized source curvature and C2 assumptions, produce the measurable uniquely stationary proximal point and the true affine standardized posterior; prove canonical KL finite, canonical llr L1 and only AE equality with the literal logdensity, actual residual L1 and both exact real entropy identities for every eta&gt;0.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[p_s+\eta_s\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\quad\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)&lt;\infty,\quad\log\frac{dr_s}{d\gamma}=\log q_s\quad r_s\text{-a.e.},\quad\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)=\int q_s\log q_s\,d\gamma=-\mathbb E_{r_s}\rho_s-\log Z_s.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Keep one actual posterior and its proved density domains</strong><p>Reuse the true posterior square-root producer once. It constructs the same measurable p, residual rho, true RGO R and affine standardized r used throughout this theorem. Its positive actual Z, actual probability and qlogq L1 are conclusions, not source inputs.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Derive stationary uniqueness from the actual source curvature</strong><p>The Hessian lower bound produces strong convexity and hence nonnegative gradient monotonicity. Subtract two stationary equations and take inner product with z-p. Positive eta forces norm(z-p)=0. This derived uniqueness permits future identification of independently constructed stationary witnesses; no witness equality is assumed here.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Transfer the genuine entropy domain to the actual tilted law</strong><p>Positivity of the already proved actual integral Z rules out a nonintegrable exponential. qlogq L1 gives exp(-rho)logq L1 by multiplying with Z, and the actual tilted integrability equivalence gives logq L1r. Since logq=-rho-logZ everywhere and r is probability, rho is L1r as well.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Use the existing canonical KL producer and AE log-ratio adapter</strong><p>Apply the shared TiltedKL theorem to the actual Gaussian base with exponents -rho and0; the zero tilt is gamma. The separately compiled log-ratio adapter identifies canonical llr with logq only r-a.e. This transfers L1 and integrals, and proves extended KL is not infinity. It supplies no pointwise RN derivative.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Integrate both exact entropy formulas under the same laws</strong><p>The actual tilted integral rewrites integral_r logq to integral_gamma qlogq. Its everywhere explicit logarithm and the proved rho/constant L1 domains give -integral_r rho-logZ. The canonical finite KL real value equals both. No original V partition, Gaussian-volume constant or affine Jacobian is added to this relative Gaussian formula.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>Complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, including dimension zero; canonical volume and covariance-I Gaussian.</li><li>Source kappa&gt;=1 and actual global C2 V with Hessian kappa^-1 I..I; positive eta. No supplied selector, probability, normalizer, integrability, entropy, LSI/T2 or final comparison certificate.</li><li>Authored measurable family S with measurable eta/y, every eta(s)&gt;0. Constant Unit specializes printed fixed parameters. Stationary uniqueness is an internally proved conclusion.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Keep one actual posterior and its proved density domains</h4><p>Reuse the true posterior square-root producer once. It constructs the same measurable p, residual rho, true RGO R and affine standardized r used throughout this theorem. Its positive actual Z, actual probability and qlogq L1 are conclusions, not source inputs.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[R_s=\mu^{[-\|x-y_s\|^2/(2\eta_s)]},\quad r_s=(x\mapsto\eta_s^{-1/2}(x-p_s))_\#R_s=\gamma^{[-\rho_s]},\quad q_s=e^{-\rho_s}/Z_s,\quad0&lt;Z_s\le1.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Derive stationary uniqueness from the actual source curvature</h4><p>The Hessian lower bound produces strong convexity and hence nonnegative gradient monotonicity. Subtract two stationary equations and take inner product with z-p. Positive eta forces norm(z-p)=0. This derived uniqueness permits future identification of independently constructed stationary witnesses; no witness equality is assumed here.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\langle\nabla V(z)-\nabla V(p),z-p\rangle\ge\kappa^{-1}\|z-p\|^2\ge0,\quad0=\|z-p\|^2+\eta\langle\nabla V(z)-\nabla V(p),z-p\rangle\Longrightarrow z=p.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower; StrongConvexFirstOrder.gradient_inner_lower_bound_of_strongConvexOn; actual hzero/hi</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Transfer the genuine entropy domain to the actual tilted law</h4><p>Positivity of the already proved actual integral Z rules out a nonintegrable exponential. qlogq L1 gives exp(-rho)logq L1 by multiplying with Z, and the actual tilted integrability equivalence gives logq L1r. Since logq=-rho-logZ everywhere and r is probability, rho is L1r as well.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\log q_s=-\rho_s-\log Z_s,\quad e^{-\rho_s}\log q_s=Z_s q_s\log q_s,\quad\log q_s\in L^1(r_s),\quad\rho_s\in L^1(r_s).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>integral_undef contradiction with actual positiveZ; Real.log_div; integrable_tilted_iff; actual he.const_mul/hlogi/hρi</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Use the existing canonical KL producer and AE log-ratio adapter</h4><p>Apply the shared TiltedKL theorem to the actual Gaussian base with exponents -rho and0; the zero tilt is gamma. The separately compiled log-ratio adapter identifies canonical llr with logq only r-a.e. This transfers L1 and integrals, and proves extended KL is not infinity. It supplies no pointwise RN derivative.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\operatorname{llr}(r_s,\gamma)=\log q_s\quad r_s\text{-a.e.},\quad\operatorname{llr}(r_s,\gamma)\in L^1(r_s),\quad\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)&lt;\infty.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>TiltedKL.finite_klDiv_and_toReal_eq_integral_normalizedLogRatio; TiltedLogRatio.llr_tilted_tilted_ae; actual hrep/hzeroTilt</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>5. Integrate both exact entropy formulas under the same laws</h4><p>The actual tilted integral rewrites integral_r logq to integral_gamma qlogq. Its everywhere explicit logarithm and the proved rho/constant L1 domains give -integral_r rho-logZ. The canonical finite KL real value equals both. No original V partition, Gaussian-volume constant or affine Jacobian is added to this relative Gaussian formula.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\mathrm{KL}(r_s\Vert\gamma)=\int\log q_s\,dr_s=\int q_s\log q_s\,d\gamma=-\int\rho_s\,dr_s-\log Z_s.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>integral_tilted; integral_sub; integral_neg; integral_const; actual hkl/hwint/hentropy</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy"><summary>Lean statement · standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy</summary><p>Under unchanged normalized source curvature and C2 assumptions, produce the measurable uniquely stationary proximal point and the true affine standardized posterior; prove canonical KL finite, canonical llr L1 and only AE equality with the literal logdensity, actual residual L1 and both exact real entropy identities for every eta&gt;0.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      (∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      let gamma := stdGaussian E
      let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
      let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
      ∀ s, r s ≪ gamma ∧
        _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧
        Integrable (MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma) (r s) ∧
        MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma =ᵐ[r s] (fun u =&gt; Real.log (q s u)) ∧
        Integrable (rho s) (r s) ∧
        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =
          (∫ u, q s u*Real.log (q s u) ∂gamma) ∧
        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =
          -(∫ u, rho s u ∂r s)-Real.log (Z s)</code></pre><p><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgorelativeentropy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy"><summary>Lean proof · standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy</summary><p>Keep one actual posterior and its proved density domains; Derive stationary uniqueness from the actual source curvature; Transfer the genuine entropy domain to the actual tilted law; Use the existing canonical KL producer and AE log-ratio adapter; Integrate both exact entropy formulas under the same laws</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy
    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}
    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)
    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧
      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)
    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)
    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 &lt; eta s) :
    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧
      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧
      (∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s) ∧
      let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
      let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
      let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
      let gamma := stdGaussian E
      let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
      let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
      ∀ s, r s ≪ gamma ∧
        _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧
        Integrable (MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma) (r s) ∧
        MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma =ᵐ[r s] (fun u =&gt; Real.log (q s u)) ∧
        Integrable (rho s) (r s) ∧
        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =
          (∫ u, q s u*Real.log (q s u) ∂gamma) ∧
        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal =
          -(∫ u, rho s u ∂r s)-Real.log (Z s) := by
  obtain ⟨p,hpm,hstat,hdata⟩ :=
    StandardizedRGOSqrtDensity.standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain hκ hV hH heta hy hpos
  have hsc := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HessianStrongConvexity.strongConvexOn_univ_of_fderiv2_lower
    hV (fun x v =&gt; (hH x v).1)
  have hunique : ∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s := by
    intro s z hz
    have hm := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.StrongConvexFirstOrder.gradient_inner_lower_bound_of_strongConvexOn
      hsc (fun w _ =&gt; (hV.differentiable (by norm_num) w).hasGradientAt)
      (x := p s) (y := z) (Set.mem_univ _) (Set.mem_univ _)
    have hg : 0 ≤ inner ℝ (gradient V z-gradient V (p s)) (z-p s) :=
      le_trans (mul_nonneg (inv_nonneg.mpr (by linarith : 0 ≤ κ)) (sq_nonneg _)) hm
    have hzero : z-p s+eta s • (gradient V z-gradient V (p s))=0 := by
      calc
        _=(z+eta s • gradient V z)-(p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)) := by module
        _=0 := by rw [hz,hstat s,sub_self]
    have hi := congrArg (fun w =&gt; inner ℝ w (z-p s)) hzero
    simp only [inner_add_left,inner_smul_left,real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq,
      inner_zero_left,starRingEnd_apply,star_trivial] at hi
    have hn : ‖z-p s‖=0 := by
      nlinarith [mul_nonneg (hpos s).le hg,norm_nonneg (z-p s)]
    exact sub_eq_zero.mp (norm_eq_zero.mp hn)
  let rho := fun s u =&gt; V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-
    Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u
  let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -V x)
  let R := fun s =&gt; mu.tilted (fun x =&gt; -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))
  let r := fun s =&gt; (R s).map (fun x =&gt; (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))
  let gamma := stdGaussian E
  let Z := fun s =&gt; ∫ u, Real.exp (-rho s u) ∂gamma
  let q := fun s u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)/Z s
  refine ⟨p,hpm,hstat,hunique,?_⟩
  change ∀ s, r s ≪ gamma ∧ _
  change ∀ s, 0 &lt; Z s ∧ Z s ≤ 1 ∧ _ at hdata
  intro s
  obtain ⟨hZ,_hZone,hr,_hwith,hprob,_hfq,_hqone,_hf,_hflp,_hfglp,_hρlp,
    he,_hdf,_hdlog,_henergy⟩ := hdata s
  change r s=gamma.tilted (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) at hr
  change Integrable (fun u =&gt; q s u*Real.log (q s u)) gamma at he
  let _ : IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) := hprob
  have hmV : Measurable V := hV.continuous.measurable
  have hρm : Measurable (rho s) := by dsimp only [rho]; fun_prop
  have hfi : Integrable (fun u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u)) gamma := by
    by_contra h
    have hzero : Z s=0 := integral_undef h
    exact hZ.ne&#x27; hzero
  have hgi : Integrable (fun _ : E =&gt; Real.exp (0 : ℝ)) gamma := by
    simp only [Real.exp_zero]
    exact integrable_const _
  have hlog (u : E) : Real.log (q s u)= -rho s u-Real.log (Z s) := by
    dsimp only [q]
    rw [Real.log_div (Real.exp_ne_zero _) hZ.ne&#x27;,Real.log_exp]
  have hw : Integrable (fun u =&gt; Real.exp (-rho s u) • Real.log (q s u)) gamma := by
    convert! he.const_mul (Z s) using 1
    funext u
    simp only [smul_eq_mul,q]
    field_simp [hZ.ne&#x27;]
  have hlogi : Integrable (fun u =&gt; Real.log (q s u)) (r s) := by
    rw [hr]
    exact (integrable_tilted_iff hfi _).mpr hw
  have hρi : Integrable (rho s) (r s) := by
    convert! hlogi.neg.sub (integrable_const (Real.log (Z s))) using 1
    funext u
    change rho s u= -Real.log (q s u)-Real.log (Z s)
    rw [hlog]
    ring
  have hrep : (fun u : E =&gt; -rho s u-Real.log (∫ z,Real.exp (-rho s z) ∂gamma)-
      (0 : ℝ)+Real.log (∫ _ : E,Real.exp (0 : ℝ) ∂gamma))=
      (fun u =&gt; Real.log (q s u)) := by
    funext u
    simp only [Real.exp_zero,integral_const,smul_eq_mul,sub_zero]
    have hmass : gamma.real Set.univ=1 := by simp [Measure.real]
    rw [hmass,one_mul,Real.log_one,add_zero]
    exact (hlog u).symm
  have hzeroTilt : gamma.tilted (fun _ : E =&gt; (0 : ℝ))=gamma := by simp
  have hkl := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.InformationTheory.TiltedKL.finite_klDiv_and_toReal_eq_integral_normalizedLogRatio
    gamma (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) (fun _ =&gt; 0) hρm.neg hfi hgi
    (by simpa only [hrep,← hr] using hlogi)
  have hkl&#x27; : _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧
      (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal=
        ∫ u,Real.log (q s u) ∂r s := by
    simpa only [hzeroTilt,← hr,hrep] using hkl
  have hae := AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.InformationTheory.TiltedLogRatio.llr_tilted_tilted_ae
    gamma (fun u =&gt; -rho s u) (fun _ =&gt; 0) hρm.neg hfi hgi
  have hae&#x27; : MeasureTheory.llr (r s) gamma =ᵐ[r s] (fun u =&gt; Real.log (q s u)) := by
    simpa only [hzeroTilt,← hr,hrep] using hae
  have hac : r s ≪ gamma := by rw [hr]; exact tilted_absolutelyContinuous _ _
  have hwint : (∫ u,Real.log (q s u) ∂r s)=
      (∫ u,q s u*Real.log (q s u) ∂gamma) := by
    rw [hr,integral_tilted]
    rfl
  have hentropy : (∫ u,Real.log (q s u) ∂r s)=
      -(∫ u,rho s u ∂r s)-Real.log (Z s) := by
    calc
      _=(∫ u,-rho s u-Real.log (Z s) ∂r s) := integral_congr_ae (Filter.Eventually.of_forall hlog)
      _=_ := by
        have hn : Integrable (fun u : E =&gt; -rho s u) (r s) := hρi.neg
        have hc : Integrable (fun _ : E =&gt; Real.log (Z s)) (r s) := integrable_const _
        rw [integral_sub hn hc,integral_neg,integral_const]
        simp [Measure.real]
  exact ⟨hac,hkl&#x27;.1,hlogi.congr hae&#x27;.symm,hae&#x27;,hρi,
    hkl&#x27;.2.trans hwint,hkl&#x27;.2.trans hentropy⟩

end
end AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy</code></pre><p><a href="../../../modules/autosamplingtheory-examplecases-smoothedpicardhmc-standardizedrgorelativeentropy.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><section data-source-comparison="AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGORelativeEntropy.standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_finite_entropy"><h3>Source assumptions versus formal assumptions</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Actual Lean</th><th>Difference kind</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Normalized source C2/Hessian bounds and eta&gt;0.</td><td>Complete finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, including dimension zero; canonical volume and covariance-I Gaussian.
